{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">2000 AMC 12 #13</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">2000 AMC 10 #22</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Constraints)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Constraints)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Guess_and_check)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Guess and check)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Fast_and_Easy)_~_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (Fast and Easy) ~ Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Sidenote\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Sidenote</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One morning each member of Angela's family drank an 8-ounce mixture of coffee with milk. The amounts of coffee and milk varied from cup to cup, but were never zero. Angela drank a quarter of the total amount of milk and a sixth of the total amount of coffee. How many people are in the family?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf64a3465c1575018dd08738c3f5e8358e87749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text {(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\text {(C)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text {(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text {(E)}\\ 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Angela drank <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the milk and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the coffee, she would have drunk <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the ingredients.  However, she actually drank <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the coffee, so she drank less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the ingredients.\n</p><p>Similarly, if she drank <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the milk and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the coffee, she would have drunk <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the ingredients.  However, she actually drank <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the milk, so she drank more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the ingredients.\n</p><p>If there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> people in the family, then each person drank <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" /> of the ingredients.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddacadafc17513d548c8a1784d413f82cad56574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} &lt; \\frac{1}{n} &lt; \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/97001255a0380ffcbd29f97b9503f6dd6577cf55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 &lt; n &lt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c913a3c933becd3814c3cc701151d6f7e91f8caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the total amount of coffee, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> of milk, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> the number of people in the family. Then each person drinks the same total amount of coffee and milk (8 ounces), so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a018ae1614ac885a782067b85a8b65ff51f73dca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{c}{6} + \\frac{m}{4}\\right)p = c + m\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"33\" />\nRegrouping, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b2f3ce3fb07a9ac2a9c3fbfa12559267bfb9608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c(6-p)=3m(p-4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />. Since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b67f50b2f802721ac352b120c0ce08ab896da12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> are positive, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67de05a1140969e355ec199f293c966743f842fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14cf5179a108302261f28d4b2335cd80085ec18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> are also positive, which is only possible when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e974dc94ca8810af030c32ed5b99fe42aa63657f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 5\\ \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Again, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421dbe5ac249bea2c9d25145a7eb9b73644c5c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed17364b06ad42c2450df4d0f6a0f06034086bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the total amount of coffee, total amount of milk, and number of people in the family, respectively. Then the total amount that is drunk is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7e9e1cae43325f2e003ca06e67a2caa3fc5398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8p,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e724486af8d468be30c650676eb4cd71b234b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+m.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8226c6019a80caf08c62c4a11dd78756b0998b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+m = 8p,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809c1c314c4a012107ac59741da7c2091a616e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 8p-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4614d78fff5a701e6118ad2c93938169f4991b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 8p-m.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We also know that the amount Angela drank, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af7c101403e55fe41cea80063666c5363b078993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{6} + \\frac{m}{4},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"34\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ounces, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d920fa2d824bcd9bd335d76088e446596842ce2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{6} + \\frac{m}{4} = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"33\" /> Rearranging gives  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55ed719f8039897e801ab7d845a0176a8896e798.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24p - c = 96.\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> Now notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c60c289e0343a236653229b2132befdfeabd04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> (by the problem statement). In addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e7702a8d9e0466c22922d4434c5adf955894d78b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b5362d959fedc2a76a8300e3300eba66303bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 8p-m &lt; 8p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/75150a5a6d47a3f779e890b69ec75aa9a56c4941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; c &lt; 8p,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea309d779e82b33b20fe99b082e83bb4224d5d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24p &gt; 24p-c &gt; 16p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"163\" height=\"16\" /> We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c387262a7e8c091353b982eb9b4572780f6a047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24p-c = 96,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c8daf82642c39dabd2b9d15639a682ae930029.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24p &gt; 96 &gt; 16p.\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> From the leftmost inequality, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae928b0a6dd027909aa7564005530abbf6cf440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> and from the rightmost inequality, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc03234ddc39e4e45b801b0d7fd1c49695be54e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &lt; 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> The only possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e974dc94ca8810af030c32ed5b99fe42aa63657f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 5\\ \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421dbe5ac249bea2c9d25145a7eb9b73644c5c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed17364b06ad42c2450df4d0f6a0f06034086bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the total amount of coffee, total amount of milk, and number of people in the family, respectively. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> obviously can't be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \nWe know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/505cc63fdfc3b44b83efaaf3af2d6f027b0adcef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{6} + \\frac{m}{4} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"33\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f738f5292875b3069544d0e1405b141a467a4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c + 3m = 96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732b50d5ea5634db96b018d5a399f8b7684791d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + m = 8p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf4ea23df0dfe7cdc94844beea6576a90036256.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c + 2m = 16p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />. \nThen, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cfe7b656b53f1e3ae744c1d27860a9c93432ae0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2c + 2m) + m = 16p + m = 96\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379cf9d64e48f41daf7fba0348da97c74782a3c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367f6b15d47102fd8fdfc1bafed72c1daeadb35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are both divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> must also be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b948c409dd8996b158c52c92954c52a3e7c7f0c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 16k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/81885324dcb5171a48db46e371402fcde80e9f22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(16k) + 2c = 48k + 2c = 96\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can't be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can't be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd0bc222cdab1211899c6b54db0db950fd7df75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/7392ef7b322191ee7c280ebcc68fcd4bcd58c3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aeb28cf7fbab29030a13d78fc0d0bb834695daa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + m = 24 + 16 = 40 = 8p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e974dc94ca8810af030c32ed5b99fe42aa63657f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 5\\ \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the total amounts of milk and coffee, respectively. In order to know the number of people, we first need to find the total amount of mixture <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a1da758f527cb6e2a972fc1e4bdf0807f15716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = m + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />. We are given that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb5824bb60826d4061a8a1344518200836633e66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{m}{4} + \\frac{c}{6} = 8\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"33\" />\nMultiplying the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yields \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663bda39c88cbc67c4528c89e8394965e11076eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m + \\frac{2}{3}c = (m + c) - \\frac{1}{3}c = t - \\frac{1}{3}c = 32\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"37\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/750591f25998a252eab22bcea31aa036f6b9e098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}c &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7225884c3e40848bfbe4c0d5d9d10ab31c0194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t &gt; 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />. Now multiplying the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yields \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99e9b3741eace27834b9465ac373e9c757aaeb16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{2}m + c = (m+c) + \\frac{1}{2}m = t + \\frac{1}{2}m = 48\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"37\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5c926e0b57bef563af94b437951a34934dee92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}m &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41d8515f91cf564bd180801fd10bebe93bc3983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t &lt; 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d32930ab578bc2550cb53925342def72bd56e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 &lt; t &lt; 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the only possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> in that range is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1fe536a6f428ba9d44dd738a5c7933c42c52fc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{8} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" /> people in Angela's family. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2484f88154fadcf9c781bba19becdae88696b77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Constraints.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Constraints)\">Solution 6 (Constraints)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Constraints)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If there were 4 people in the family, and each of them drank exactly the same amount of coffee and milk as Angela, there would be too much coffee. If there were 6 people in the family, and each of them drank exactly the same amount of coffee and milk as Angela, there would be not enough milk. Thus, it has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897a203bdf45af36f2b9edc59c3bc0beeb898be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>(But how can we assume that each of them drank exactly the same amount of coffee and milk?)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Guess_and_check.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Guess_and_check)\">Solution 7 (Guess and check)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Guess and check)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of ounces that Angela's family drank has to be a multiple of 8, so we can find the right answer by guessing random values for the number of ounces of coffee and milk Angela drank. With Angela drinking 4 ounces of milk and 4 ounces of coffee, we get 40 total ounces Angela's family drank. Dividing that by 8(each person drank 8 ounces) we get 5 members who drank the coffee with milk, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />  ~ Mathyguy88\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/G4c2oCtupTg?si=SwV2TLJ1EWeE6EeW&amp;t=422\">https://youtu.be/G4c2oCtupTg?si=SwV2TLJ1EWeE6EeW&amp;t=422</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Fast_and_Easy.29_.7E_Pi_Academy\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Fast_and_Easy)_~_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution 2 (Fast and Easy) ~ Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (Fast and Easy) ~ Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UGcqyhh03LQ?si=WKAVn2VitpmeCvSd\">https://youtu.be/UGcqyhh03LQ?si=WKAVn2VitpmeCvSd</a> ~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/k6G5BjjILGY\">https://youtu.be/k6G5BjjILGY</a>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OT42J21ZNC8&amp;feature=youtu.be\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OT42J21ZNC8&amp;feature=youtu.be</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7QU8OlnljHw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7QU8OlnljHw</a>     ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_MRENTHUSIASM_.28English-Chinese_Bilingual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\">Video Solution 4 by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/d6kW4-fmPeA\">https://youtu.be/d6kW4-fmPeA</a>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sidenote\">Sidenote</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Sidenote\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we now solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9838027fb25854115044943990e6236bece06f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a08cbb7c24b5171f90116bff95d6218e0a191b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. Thus in total the family drank <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces of milk and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces of coffee. Angela drank exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ounces of milk and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ounces of coffee.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12\">2000 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" ti